  <data name="Rule_MaxDailyWorkingTime_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Daily working time</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_MaxDailyWorkingTime_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A working day is capped at 8 hours. It may reach 10 hours if the average over 24 weeks (six months) comes back to 8. A shift longer than that is cut.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_Breaks_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Breaks</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_Breaks_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>More than 6 hours of work owe 30 minutes of break, more than 9 hours owe 45, in pieces of at least 15 minutes — and never more than 6 hours in a row without one. Breaks are carved out of the shift; a running operation pauses and resumes.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_RestPeriod_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rest period</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_RestPeriod_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Between two working days a crew gets 11 uninterrupted hours of rest (10 in a few named sectors). A shift that would start too soon after the crew's previous one is delayed.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_NightWork_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Night work</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_NightWork_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A shift with more than 2 hours between 23:00 and 06:00 is night work and is capped at 8 hours (10 with monthly averaging), even where the day cap is 10.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_SundayRest_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sunday rest</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_SundayRest_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>No work from 00:00 to 24:00 on Sundays unless a § 10 exception applies. Multi-shift plants may move that window by up to 6 hours.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_HolidayRest_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Public holidays</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_HolidayRest_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The same ban applies to public holidays. Which days those are is set by the federal state — nine apply everywhere, the rest differ.</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_FreeSundays_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Free Sundays</value></data>
  <data name="Rule_FreeSundays_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Even where Sunday work is permitted, at least 15 Sundays a year must stay free. A pattern that staffs every Sunday is reported.</value></data>
